<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gelderland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Guelderland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gelderland is a province in the east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnhem">Arnhem</a>. It descends from the medieval county and later Duchy of Guelders, which Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> acquired in 1543. As one of the seven provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> it had a vote in the States General, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veluwe">Veluwe</a> heathland and fertile river lands made it largely agricultural. In 1672 French armies overran it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gelderland.jpg" alt="Gelderland" width="320" height="361" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gelderland_in_the_Netherlands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
